CALL newPutForth(148, 1, 'De-escalation training is good — talk first, force only when necessary. Good officers already do this. Just don\'t mandate it in ways that get officers killed when the situation demands decisive action.');
CALL newPutForth(149, 1, 'Crisis intervention, de-escalation, use-of-force continuum — these belong in every academy. Most officers operate this way already. The exceptions need correction, not the whole institution.');
CALL newPutForth(153, 1, 'Of course police should try other means before using lethal force. No good officer wants to pull that trigger. Problem is Monday-morning quarterbacking every split-second decision made under life-threatening pressure.');
CALL newPutForth(154, 1, 'You see a fellow officer abusing someone, you step in. That\'s not squealing — that\'s the job. Vast majority of officers would do it. The blue wall of silence is a real problem, but it\'s not universal.');
CALL newPutForth(165, 1, 'Fund police, train them better, hold the bad actors accountable. Don\'t demonize the whole institution over a handful. Unions protect officers from political persecution — that\'s their function.');
CALL newPutForth(166, 1, 'Policing doesn\'t need to be abolished — the oversight mechanisms need to be strengthened. Body cameras, better training, civilian review boards with real authority. Fix the checks, not the institution.');
CALL newPutForth(167, 1, 'Abolishing the prison system would put dangerous people back on the streets with nowhere to go. The people who want to abolish prisons don\'t live next door to the people who\'d be walking free.');
CALL newPutForth(168, 1, 'Reform prisons — reduce overcrowding, expand rehabilitation, fix solitary abuse. But abolishing incarceration would create chaos. Improve the system, don\'t burn it down without a replacement.');
CALL newPutForth(178, 1, 'Prison exists to keep dangerous people away from the law-abiding public. When we release prisoners early or without rehabilitation, we transfer risk from criminals to every innocent person they encounter.');
CALL newPutForth(219, 1, 'Qualified immunity exists because officers make life-and-death calls in seconds. If every judgment call opened them to personal bankruptcy through lawsuits, nobody would take the job. That\'s the tradeoff.');
CALL newPutForth(545, 1, 'Punishment should fit the crime and be realistic. Bail set at $100,000 for a petty offense isn\'t justice — it\'s a wealth tax on getting out. But bail for violent crimes protects the community.');
CALL newPutForth(561, 1, 'Back the blue, full stop. These men and women run toward danger when every instinct says run away. They deserve our support, not protesters outside their precincts calling them murderers.');
CALL newPutForth(594, 1, 'No-knock raids on nonviolent drug warrants, asset forfeiture without conviction — these are real abuses of police power. Conservatives should be first to call them out. That\'s not anti-cop, that\'s pro-liberty.');
CALL newPutForth(602, 1, 'BLM protests achieved what, exactly? Crime went up. Cops retired early. Recruitment collapsed. The cities that embraced defund demands have worse crime numbers now than before. That\'s not reform.');
CALL newPutForth(778, 1, 'Some crimes are so heinous that death is the only just response. A serial killer, a child murderer, a mass terrorist — keeping them alive for fifty years at public expense is its own injustice.');
CALL newPutForth(1169, 1, 'Seen it myself — some officers abuse the badge. Treat every traffic stop like an interrogation, power-trip on ordinary citizens. That\'s a training and culture problem. The good cops hate it too.');
CALL newPutForth(1170, 1, 'Police academies teach tactics and law but often fail to distinguish between authority — which comes from community consent — and mere power, which comes from a badge and a gun. Critical difference.');
CALL newPutForth(1171, 1, 'Warrior mindset has a time and place — when lives are at stake. Problem is when it becomes the default for every encounter, including routine traffic stops. That\'s how trust erodes.');
CALL newPutForth(1173, 1, 'If police carry AR-15s on patrol, law-abiding citizens should be able to own the same. Equal protection under the law goes both ways. Don\'t set one standard for officers and another for civilians.');
CALL newPutForth(1187, 1, 'Pulling someone over for a cracked taillight or an air freshener is pretextual policing that destroys trust. Limit traffic stops to real violations — speeding, DUI, reckless driving. That\'s the boundary.');
CALL newPutForth(1410, 1, 'Officer safety is the first priority. A dead officer protects no one. Every policy demand has to be evaluated against what it does to officer safety. That\'s not optional — it\'s the baseline.');
CALL newPutForth(1411, 1, 'Officers put their lives on the line for us every day. The very least we owe them is having their backs — proper equipment, legal support, fair pay, community respect, and contract protections.');
CALL newPutForth(1600, 1, 'More than 185 people on death row have been exonerated since 1973. That should give everyone pause. Reserve capital punishment for cases where evidence is absolutely ironclad. But that\'s not an argument to abolish it.');




